# React + TypeScript

- Vite SPA. Client components only. No Next.js, no `"use client"`, no `next/link` or `next/image`.
- Keep the landing as one `App` composed from `src/components/landing` and `src/components/layout`.
- Use named exports. Colocate interactive state in the component that owns it (hero slider, mobile nav).
- Prefer CSS transitions over per-frame React state (hero progress bar, Ken Burns, reveals).
- Use `useRevealOnScroll` for `.reveal-up` — do not hardcode `.revealed` on first paint.
- No cart, prices, or CMS fetches in this phase.

```tsx
// ✅ client React
export function Hero() {
  const [active, setActive] = useState(0)
  return <section className="hero">...</section>
}
```
